================================================================================================================
Laya
================================================================================================================

Autopilot's model is a fine-tune of Laya (multilingual checkpoint), https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
Copyright Convai Innovations. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).

  - crates/reins-core/src/autopilot/sequence.rs is a port to Rust of Laya's input sequence builder
    (`rl_common.build_sequence`), modified for Autopilot's fixed question; tools/laya/sequence.py is a reference
    implementation of the same.
  - tools/laya/ loads, fine-tunes and exports Laya checkpoints (Laya itself is downloaded, not included).
  - The published model packages (not in this repository) are derived from Laya's weights.


================================================================================================================
mmBERT-base
================================================================================================================

Laya's multilingual checkpoint, and so the Autopilot model, is built on mmBERT-base,
https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base, by the Johns Hopkins University Center for Language and Speech
Processing (JHU CLSP). Licensed under the MIT License (model card: "license: mit").
